1
00:00:00,155 --> 00:00:01,825
(Sheldon:)I'm truly worried.

2
00:00:01,823 --> 00:00:04,663
I-I told you, there's
nothing to worry about.

3
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,460
(Sheldon:)Well, I've been
doing some research

4
00:00:06,461 --> 00:00:08,791
(Sheldon:)and I've learned that
one in 700,000 people

5
00:00:08,797 --> 00:00:11,127
die from general anesthesia.

6
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:13,803
Buddy, w... Do you realize that
that also means

7
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:17,542
(Leonard:)699,999 people don't die?

8
00:00:19,975 --> 00:00:21,405
(Sheldon:)I suppose that's true.

9
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:25,708
(Sheldon:)You're such a glass
half-full kind of guy.

10
00:00:27,649 --> 00:00:29,919
(Sheldon:)I'm going to miss that.

11
00:00:32,521 --> 00:00:35,991
(Raj:)Oh, so, my, uh, parents'
40th anniversary's coming up

12
00:00:35,991 --> 00:00:38,161
(Raj:)and I can't think
of a thing to get them.

13
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:39,490
(Howard:)Damn, can you imagine

14
00:00:39,494 --> 00:00:43,234
(Howard:)being married to someone
for 40 years?

15
00:00:46,168 --> 00:00:47,968
(Bernadette:)Not anymore.

16
00:00:52,407 --> 00:00:54,677
(Raj:)Anyway, any ideas on a gift?

17
00:00:54,676 --> 00:00:56,876
(Bernadette:)Well, what are some
of the things they like?

18
00:00:56,878 --> 00:00:59,348
(Raj:)They used to like
going to the Mumbai Symphony,

19
00:00:59,348 --> 00:01:01,678
(Raj:)but last year my mom thought
they were phoning it in.

